  "prototype": {
    "name": "ofi_persist_x_spread_z",
    "mechanism": "Stress-gated flow COMMITMENT measured by run structure, not magnitude: ofi_sign_persist_60s scores the fraction of consecutive ofi_15s readings keeping the same sign, signed by the current direction -- a magnitude-blind second-order statistic. Gating it by the spread-state z asks whether the COST of commitment is what makes it informative: under WIDE stressed spreads, keeping one-sided book flow running snapshot after snapshot bears full adverse-selection cost, so such commitment is deliberate informed accumulation -> continuation at 15-60s; under unusually TIGHT quotes the same sign runs are zero-cost churn (product flips them). Because the base ignores flow size entirely, this tests whether pure run STRUCTURE carries the stress-informed signal -- a different economic input than ofi_concord_x_spread_z (magnitude-capped agreement) and than ofi_z_x_spread_z (flow surprise).",
    "info_set": "ofi_15s, quoted_spread_ticks",
    "inspiration": "iter-003 R4-A fill-in brief: ofi_sign_persist_60s (R3-C admitted) has no spread-z interaction yet; CKS (2014) OFI persistence interacted with the round-3 live gating dimension. Dedup note: the base sits on the round-3 watchlist (panel rho 0.782, rho 0.723 vs ofi_concord_15_60); the gated forms decorrelate empirically (0.22-0.42 for round-3 products) but sibling corr with the ofi_concord gates needs screening.",
